          %h2#locally_indexed_categories Locally indexed categories
          %p
            The presheaf category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [V^{op}, Set]
            is also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([V^{op}, Set], \times, 1)
            is called
            %strong
              locally
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Levy19"} Levy (2019)
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Levy19"} Levy 2019
          %p
            As we have stated the definitions, this is trivial, but both concepts have more elementary reformulations that avoid
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/size+issues"} size issues
          %p
            For example, with
            %a{:href => "#Levy19"} Levy (2019), slide 21
            this gives an abstract proof of the standard fact that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+categories"} simplicially enriched categories
            can be viewed as those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            which take value in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity-on-objects+functors"} identity-on-objects functors
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Riehl23"} Riehl (2023), Prop. 1.2.3
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman13"} Shulman 2013
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Locally graded categories were introduced as
            %strong
              large
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Wood"}> Richard Wood
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Indicial methods for relative categories
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/10222/55465"} hdl:10222/55465
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Wood"}> Richard Wood
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                    \-indexed categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Indexed Categories and Their Applications
                %strong 661
                (1978) 126-140 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/BFb0061362"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0061362
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Wood"}> Richard Wood
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em re: module for a category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+mailing+list"} categories mailing list
              (2003) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/punkdit/categories/blob/26b751bbcbe6765fe447e805629ff6416f4c38b1/gmane/science/mathematics/categories/2425"}> link
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p For the terminology we use see:
          %ul
            %li#Levy19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Blain+Levy"}> Paul Blain Levy
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Locally graded categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~pbl/papers/locgrade.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Levy-LocallyGradedCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+McDermott"}> Dylan McDermott
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarmo+Uustalu"} Tarmo Uustalu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Flexibly graded monads and graded algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematics of Program Construction MPC 2022
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 13544
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1007/978-3-031-16912-0_4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-031-16912-0_4
          %p
            For the example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            example see for instance:
          %ul
            %li#Riehl18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
              , Prop. 1.2.3 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy coherent structures
              %strong 1
              (2023) 1-31 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.07404"}> arXiv:1801.07404
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac//expositions/articles/1/te1abs.html"} tac:te1
          %p
            A generalisation of locally graded categories to skew-enrichment may be found in the following under the name
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong skew-proactegories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Campbell"}> Alexander Campbell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Skew-enriched categories
          %p
            For a treatment of
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            by means of locally graded categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rory+Lucyshyn-Wright"}> Rory Lucyshyn-Wright
              ,
              %em V-graded categories and V-W-bigraded categories: Functor categories and bifunctors over non-symmetric bases
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.18557"}> arXiv:2502.18557
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+colimits"} weighted colimits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limits"} weighted limits
            in the context of categories enriched in a presheaf category:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+Borceux"} F. Borceux
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
            %li#Shulman13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                %em
                  Enriched indexed categories,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theory+and+Applications+of+Categories"} Theory and Applications of Categories
        .revisedby
